--- A function whose every return hands on nothing answers nothing even
--- where it can fail (a style read by `float` inside): a variable may hold
--- that answer, to ask whether it failed (parity 370), but a field holds a
--- value of its kind, and nothing is none — refused as `log[…]`'s answer
--- is. It had run interpreted, the field holding `done`, and the compiled
--- program had not built (Kite's axis width, 2026-11-07)
struct Axis[w]

fn size_of[t]
    v = float[t]
    v

fn widest[xs]
    size = size_of['12']
    out = 0.0
    for x in xs
        out = max[out, size]

a = Axis[1.5]
a.w = widest[[1, 2]]
log[a.w]
